    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Mild-mod SLE ⍉controlled on hydroxychloroquine, in pts who would otherwise be candidates for a course of corticosteroids: MTX 15-20 mg once a wk, azathioprine 2 mg/kg/day or mycophenolate mofetil 1-1.5 g twice a day can be added, to keep corticosteroids @ the lowest dose."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Belimumab (10 mg/kg IV Q2wks for 3 doses, then monthly, or 200 mg SC wkly) for uncontrolled dz or freq flares; screen and monitor for depression and suicidality."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Severe dz (eg, lupus nephritis): corticosteroids plus cyclophosphamide or mycophenolate mofetil for induction; both need effective BC. Cyclophosphamide beyond 6 months = discouraged (infertility, CA); maintenance = mycophenolate or azathioprine."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Anifrolumab (anti-type I interferon-r, 300 mg IV every 4 wks) may be added for mod-severe SLE, esp severe skin dz."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Rituximab = an option for refractory thrombocytopenia and hemolytic anemia and, w a corticosteroid, an option (anecdotal evidence) for neuropsych lupus."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
